{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q408314","formula":"C₁₅H₂₃N₅O₄","hill":"C15H23N5O4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":23.0,"N":5.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Kyotorphin","ru":"Киотрофин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Kyotorphin (L-tyrosyl-L-arginine) is a neuroactive dipeptide which plays a role in pain regulation in the brain. It was first isolated from bovine brain, by Japanese scientists in 1979. Kyotorphin was named for the site of its discovery, Kyoto, Japan and because of its morphine- (or endorphin-) like analgesic activity.","ru":"Киотрофин (L-тирозил-L-аргинин) — нейроактивный дипептид, участвующий в регуляции боли мозгом. Он был впервые изолирован в бычьем мозге японскими учёными в 1979 году. Киотрофин назвали в честь места его открытия — Киото и потому, что по своему обезболивающему действию он напоминал морфин."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":123804,"mass":337.37,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC(=CC=C1C[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCN=C(N)N)C(=O)O)N)O","inchikey":"JXNRXNCCROJZFB-RYUDHWBXSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-[[(2S)-2-amino-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanoyl]amino]-5-(diaminomethylideneamino)pentanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"123804","atoms":47,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.701,"y":1.546,"z":1.953,"el":"O"},{"x":0.166,"y":-2.018,"z":-0.927,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.635,"y":-3.262,"z":0.793,"el":"O"},{"x":5.686,"y":-2.325,"z":-0.574,"el":"O"},{"x":0.02,"y":0.195,"z":0.194,"el":"N"},{"x":0.496,"y":3.529,"z":-0.18,"el":"N"},{"x":-5.188,"y":-0.12,"z":-0.803,"el":"N"},{"x":-7.275,"y":0.195,"z":-1.76,"el":"N"},{"x":-7.149,"y":0.324,"z":0.512,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.575,"y":-0.835,"z":1.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.054,"y":-0.568,"z":1.301,"el":"C"},{"x":1.202,"y":2.254,"z":-0.31,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.94,"y":-0.494,"z":0.052,"el":"C"},{"x":2.706,"y":2.463,"z":-0.081,"el